@@ -0,0 +1,178 @@
+# Unity Catalog Compatibility
+
+!!! note
+    The Unity Catalog compatibility API is a **fork extension** (branch `multimodal-uc-objects`), not part of upstream Lakekeeper.
+
+This fork serves a **Unity Catalog-compatible REST surface** at `/api/2.1/unity-catalog` so that unmodified Unity Catalog clients can manage **Volumes**, **Functions**, and **Registered Models + Model Versions** — and obtain **temporary storage credentials** for volume files and model artifacts — against Lakekeeper. UC Catalogs and Schemas are mapped read-mostly onto existing Lakekeeper concepts: a UC *catalog* is a Lakekeeper **Warehouse** (in the caller's default project) and a UC *schema* is a **top-level Namespace** in that warehouse.
+
+The new entities are first-class Lakekeeper objects: they live in dedicated Postgres tables, participate in location-overlap checks alongside Iceberg tables, and are governed by the same per-action OpenFGA authorization model as tables and views (new object types `lakekeeper_volume`, `lakekeeper_function`, `lakekeeper_model` in authorization model v4.8).
+
+## Clients
+
+The compatibility surface is exercised end-to-end (see [Testing](#testing)) with:
+
+- **`unitycatalog-client` 0.4.1** — full CRUD for catalogs (read-only), schemas, volumes, functions, registered models and model versions, plus both temporary-credentials endpoints.
+- **`unitycatalog-ai` 0.4.0** and its framework adapters (**`unitycatalog-langchain`**, **`unitycatalog-openai`**) — `create_python_function`, function retrieval and client-side `execute_function`, LangChain `UCFunctionToolkit` tools, OpenAI tool-schema generation.
+- **Storage engines via vended credentials** — `boto3`, DuckDB (`httpfs`), and `pyarrow` reading/writing volume files and model artifacts directly on object storage with credentials from the temporary-credentials endpoints.
+
+Any client that speaks the Unity Catalog 0.x REST wire format for these resources (including the `uc` CLI's `catalog`/`schema`/`volume`/`function`/`registered_model`/`model_version` commands) should work for the operations listed below; operations the compatibility API deliberately does not support (catalog create, renames, path credentials) return a well-formed UC `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error instead of an unexpected failure.
+
+## Concept mapping
+
+| Unity Catalog | Lakekeeper | Notes |
+|---------------|------------|-------|
+| Catalog | Warehouse (in the caller's default project) | Read-only via UC API; manage warehouses via `/management/v1/warehouse`. |
+| Schema | Top-level Namespace of that warehouse | Full CRUD. The UC `comment` is stored as the namespace property `comment`. Only depth-1 namespaces are visible through the UC API. |
+| Volume | `uc_volume` entity in a namespace | `MANAGED` or `EXTERNAL`, see below. |
+| Function | `uc_function` entity in a namespace | The client's `function_info` JSON is stored verbatim (byte-fidelity round-trip). |
+| Registered Model / Model Version | `uc_model` / `uc_model_version` entities | Versions are server-assigned integers with a `PENDING_REGISTRATION → READY` lifecycle. |
+| `full_name` | `<warehouse-name>.<top-level-namespace>.<name>` | For schemas: `<warehouse-name>.<namespace>`. |
+
+**Volume locations.** `MANAGED` volumes must not carry a `storage_location`; the server derives one under the namespace location: `<namespace-location>/__uc_volumes/<volume_id>`. `EXTERNAL` volumes require a `storage_location`, which must pass the warehouse storage profile's allowed-location check. Both are validated against the warehouse-wide location-overlap check that spans Iceberg tables, views, generic tables, volumes, and model versions.
+
+**Model artifact layout.** Registered models get a managed location `<namespace-location>/__uc_models/<model_id>`; each version's artifacts live below it at `<model-location>/versions/<model_version_id>`. Clients never choose these paths — they upload artifacts directly to the version's `storage_location` using vended credentials.
+
+**Timestamps** are epoch **milliseconds** (UC convention). Errors use the UC envelope `{"error_code", "message", "details":[{"@type":"google.rpc.ErrorInfo","reason":...}]}` with statuses mapped as 400→`INVALID_ARGUMENT`, 401→`UNAUTHENTICATED`, 403→`PERMISSION_DENIED`, 404→`NOT_FOUND`, 409→`ALREADY_EXISTS`, 5xx→`INTERNAL`. Successful `DELETE`s return `{}` with HTTP 200. List endpoints paginate with `max_results`/`page_token` in and `next_page_token` out (omitted on the last page).
+
+## Endpoint reference
+
+All paths are relative to `/api/2.1/unity-catalog`.
+
+### Catalogs (read-only warehouse mapping)
+
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------|
+| GET | `/catalogs` | Lists warehouses of the caller's project, name-sorted. |
+| GET | `/catalogs/{name}` | `id` is the warehouse ID; `created_at` is omitted (warehouses do not track one). |
+| POST | `/catalogs` | **400** `INVALID_ARGUMENT` — manage warehouses via the management API. |
+| PATCH | `/catalogs/{name}` | **400** `INVALID_ARGUMENT`. |
+| DELETE | `/catalogs/{name}` | **400** `INVALID_ARGUMENT`. |
+
+### Schemas (top-level namespaces)
+
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------|
+| POST | `/schemas` | Delegates to the Iceberg namespace handlers (identical authorization, idempotency and authorizer bookkeeping). `storage_root` is rejected with **400**. |
+| GET | `/schemas?catalog_name=...` | |
+| GET | `/schemas/{full_name}` | |
+| PATCH | `/schemas/{full_name}` | `comment` and `properties` updates; `new_name` (rename) is rejected with **400**. |
+| DELETE | `/schemas/{full_name}[?force=true]` | Non-recursive drop; a non-empty schema fails with **400** (UC convention) rather than Lakekeeper's 409. |
+
+### Volumes
+
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------|
+| POST | `/volumes` | `volume_type` `MANAGED` (no `storage_location` allowed) or `EXTERNAL` (`storage_location` required). |
+| GET | `/volumes?catalog_name=...&schema_name=...` | `include_browse` is accepted and ignored. |
+| GET | `/volumes/{full_name}` | Response includes `volume_id` — the input to credential vending. |
+| PATCH | `/volumes/{full_name}` | `comment` only; `new_name` (rename) is rejected with **400**. |
+| DELETE | `/volumes/{full_name}` | Hard delete of the catalog entry; files are not purged. |
+
+### Functions
+
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------|
+| POST | `/functions` | Body is a wrapper: fields nest under `function_info` (not flat). The 14 required UC create fields are validated for presence; everything else round-trips byte-identically (`routine_definition`, `input_params.parameters` order and per-parameter fields, the `properties` JSON-string quirk). |
+| GET | `/functions?catalog_name=...&schema_name=...` | |
+| GET | `/functions/{full_name}` | Stored spec merged with server fields (`function_id`, `full_name`, `created_at`, ...). |
+| DELETE | `/functions/{full_name}` | |
+
+There is deliberately no `PATCH /functions/{full_name}`: the UC spec has no function update endpoint.
+
+### Registered Models and Model Versions
+
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------|
+| POST | `/models` | Returns the model's managed `storage_location` and stable `id`. |
+| GET | `/models` | `catalog_name`/`schema_name` are optional (list-all); `schema_name` without `catalog_name` is rejected. |
+| GET | `/models/{full_name}` | |
+| PATCH | `/models/{full_name}` | `comment` only; `new_name` is rejected with **400**. |
+| DELETE | `/models/{full_name}[?force=true]` | Without `force`, deleting a model that still has versions fails. |
+| POST | `/models/versions` | **Flat path** (UC quirk): the model is identified by body fields. Version numbers are server-assigned (`MAX(version)+1`, serialized via row locks). New versions start as `PENDING_REGISTRATION`. |
+| GET | `/models/{full_name}/versions` | |
+| GET | `/models/{full_name}/versions/{version}` | |
+| PATCH | `/models/{full_name}/versions/{version}` | `comment` only. |
+| PATCH | `/models/{full_name}/versions/{version}/finalize` | `PENDING_REGISTRATION → READY`. The body repeats `full_name` + `version` (UC contract). |
+| DELETE | `/models/{full_name}/versions/{version}` | |
+
+### Temporary credentials
+
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------|
+| POST | `/temporary-volume-credentials` | Body: `{volume_id, operation: READ_VOLUME\|WRITE_VOLUME}`. Note: takes the `volume_id` UUID, not a name. |
+| POST | `/temporary-model-version-credentials` | Body: `{catalog_name, schema_name, model_name, version, operation: READ_MODEL_VERSION\|READ_WRITE_MODEL_VERSION}`. |
+| POST | `/temporary-path-credentials` | **400** `INVALID_ARGUMENT` — not supported; use volume credentials instead. |
+
+## Credential vending
+
+Volume and model-version credentials reuse Lakekeeper's [storage profile](storage.md) vending machinery (the same code path as Iceberg and [generic table](generic-tables.md) credential vending), downscoped to the volume location or the version's artifact location:
+
+- `READ_VOLUME` / `READ_MODEL_VERSION` vend read-only credentials; `WRITE_VOLUME` / `READ_WRITE_MODEL_VERSION` vend read-write-delete credentials.
+- The response carries exactly one cloud-specific member — `aws_temp_credentials` (`access_key_id`, `secret_access_key`, `session_token`), `azure_user_delegation_sas` (`sas_token`), or `gcp_oauth_token` (`oauth_token`) — plus a top-level `expiration_time` in epoch milliseconds. `expiration_time` is omitted when the vended credentials do not expire, and credential-less profiles return an empty envelope `{}`.
+
+**Model-version lifecycle rule:** `READ_WRITE_MODEL_VERSION` credentials are only vended while the version is `PENDING_REGISTRATION` — after `finalize` the artifacts are immutable and a read-write request returns **400**. `READ_MODEL_VERSION` credentials are vended for pending and `READY` versions, but never for `FAILED_REGISTRATION`.
+
+The intended MLflow-style flow: create a version (pending) → obtain `READ_WRITE` credentials → upload artifacts to the version's `storage_location` → `finalize` → consumers obtain `READ` credentials and download.
+
+## Authorization
+
+Each entity gets its own action enum, checked through the pluggable `Authorizer` (see [Authorization](authorization.md)); `get_metadata` is the *can-see* permission, and entities the caller cannot see are masked as **404** to hide their existence:
+
+| Entity | Actions |
+|--------|---------|
+| Volume (`CatalogVolumeAction`) | `get_metadata`, `read_data`, `write_data`, `drop`, `include_in_list` |
+| Function (`CatalogFunctionAction`) | `get_metadata`, `execute`, `drop`, `include_in_list` |
+| Model (`CatalogModelAction`) | `get_metadata`, `read_data`, `write_data`, `drop`, `include_in_list`, `create_version` |
+| Namespace (additions) | `create_volume`, `list_volumes`, `create_function`, `list_functions`, `create_model`, `list_models` |
+
+**Data-plane rule.** `read_data`/`write_data` on volumes and models gate *file access* (credential vending), and are excluded from the instance-admin bypass: being a Lakekeeper administrator does not by itself grant access to volume file contents or model artifacts, mirroring the behavior for table data. All other actions are control-plane. No function action is data-plane: UC function *execution happens client-side* (the client reconstructs the callable from the stored `routine_definition`), so `execute` only gates retrieving the definition — which `get_metadata` already reveals. Treat function definition visibility as execution capability.
+
+**Model versions have no authorization identity of their own** — version operations authorize on the parent model: create/finalize/comment-update → `create_version`; version delete → `drop`; `READ` credentials → `read_data`; `READ_WRITE` credentials → `read_data` + `write_data`.
+
+### OpenFGA model (v4.8)
+
+Authorization model v4.8 adds the object types `lakekeeper_volume`, `lakekeeper_function` and `lakekeeper_model` (patterned on `lakekeeper_generic_table`), with the familiar assignable relations `ownership`, `pass_grants`, `manage_grants`, `describe`, `select`, `modify` — functions additionally have `execute` (implied by `ownership`, `modify`, or `select` on the parent namespace). Action relations derive as usual: `can_read_data` from `select`, `can_write_data`/`can_drop` from `modify`, `can_get_metadata` from `describe`, `can_create_version` from `modify`, `can_execute` from `execute`. Namespaces gain the three child types plus `can_create_volume`/`can_create_function`/`can_create_model` (from `create`) and the matching `can_list_*` relations, so permissions inherit from Namespace and Warehouse exactly like tables.
+
+Permission management uses Lakekeeper's management API (not UC "permissions" endpoints):
+
+- `GET`/`POST /management/v1/permissions/warehouse/{warehouse_id}/volume/{volume_id}/assignments`
+- `GET /management/v1/permissions/warehouse/{warehouse_id}/volume/{volume_id}/authorizer-actions`
+- ...and the same pair under `.../function/{function_id}/...` and `.../model/{model_id}/...`.
+
+Authentication is unchanged: the UC router sits inside the same authenticator middleware stack as `/catalog` and `/management`, so UC clients send the usual `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Variable | Default | Description |
+|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `LAKEKEEPER__ENABLE_UC_COMPAT_API` | `true` | Serve the Unity Catalog-compatible REST API at `/api/2.1/unity-catalog`. Set to `false` to disable the surface entirely. |
+
+## Limitations (v1)
+
+Deliberate scope cuts of the first version:
+
+- **No events, idempotency records, or endpoint statistics** for UC-specific endpoints: UC requests do not emit change events, are not covered by idempotency-key replay, and do not appear in the [endpoint statistics](monitoring.md) registry (the UC router is mounted outside the statistics middleware). Schemas are the exception — they delegate to the Iceberg namespace handlers and behave identically to that surface.
+- **Hard deletes.** UC `DELETE` on volumes, functions, models and versions removes the catalog entry immediately — no [soft-deletion](concepts.md#soft-deletion)/undrop, and no storage purge (files at the location are left in place).
+- **No `temporary-path-credentials`** (returns `INVALID_ARGUMENT`); credentials are vended per volume or model version only.
+- **No renames** of volumes, models, or schemas via the UC API (`new_name` returns `INVALID_ARGUMENT`).
+- **Catalogs are read-only**: create/update/delete return `INVALID_ARGUMENT` pointing to the management API.
+- **No UC metastore or UC-native permissions endpoints** — Lakekeeper's management API is the permission surface.
+- **JSON object key order is normalized** for stored function specs (JSONB storage): all values — strings, numbers, array order — round-trip byte-identically, but the order of keys inside JSON objects may differ from the create request. This is semantically irrelevant to JSON clients.
+- **Functions execute client-side.** Lakekeeper stores and serves the definition; it never runs function code. Consequently, anyone with `get_metadata` can read the definition (see [Authorization](#authorization)).
+
+## Testing
+
+The end-to-end suite lives in `tests/uc-compat` of the fork repository:
+
+```bash
+# full suite (MODE=allowall: authn disabled, allow-all authorizer)
+bash tests/uc-compat/run.sh
+
+# catalogs/schemas only
+bash tests/uc-compat/run.sh -m smoke
+
+# OpenFGA stack verification (migration writes the v4.8 model, authz matrix)
+MODE=openfga bash tests/uc-compat/run.sh
+```
+
+`run.sh` builds the fork binary, starts Postgres, OpenFGA and MinIO (with a non-root vending user) via docker-compose, migrates, bootstraps, creates a warehouse with an S3 storage profile pointing at MinIO, and runs pytest. The suite proves: catalog/schema read-mapping and error envelope; volume CRUD with MANAGED location derivation and EXTERNAL validation; boto3 and DuckDB access to volume files with vended (and downscoped) credentials; `unitycatalog-ai` function create + local execution and LangChain/OpenAI tool generation with byte-fidelity spec round-trips; the full model version lifecycle including the pending-only `READ_WRITE` credential rule; and, in `openfga` mode, that migration installs the v4.8 authorization model and anonymous bootstrap is rejected. See `tests/uc-compat/README.md` for modes and environment variables.
